@using Raptor21.RCL.Localization
@inject IRaptorLocalizer L

@* The card-mode filter drawer's opener, rendered by the PAGE instead of by the grid.

   WHY THIS IS A PAGE NODE AND NOT A MOVED FAB. The grid region replaces its own `outerHTML` on every
   page/sort/filter change. Anything the shell had lifted OUT of that region survives the swap while the
   server re-renders a fresh copy INSIDE it, so a "move the FAB into the menu" design leaves two openers
   behind after the first pagination — the stale one in the menu (with a stale badge) and the new one in
   the region. Declaring the opener where it lives instead means nothing is ever moved: the region owns
   the drawer, the page owns the button, and neither re-renders the other.

   WHY IT WORKS FROM OUTSIDE THE REGION. `data-rg-filter-open` carries the grid's id here. The drawer
   feature listens on the DOCUMENT and resolves ownership by that id, so the button opens exactly one
   grid's drawer no matter where in the page it sits. The valueless attribute the FAB uses keeps its old
   meaning ("the grid I am inside"), which is what a grid nested in a detail panel relies on.

   The badge is left EMPTY and `hidden` on the server. Its number is mirrored from the region's own
   `.rg-filter-count` by `runtime/grid-filter-entry.ts`, because the count changes with every region swap
   and the page markup around this button does not re-render then. Rendering a number here would show a
   stale one from the moment the first filter is applied. *@

<button type="button"
        class="rg-gridfilter-entry"
        data-rg-filter-open="@For"
        aria-label="@L["Grid_OpenColumnFilters"]">
    <span class="rg-gridfilter-ico" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="rg-gridfilter-label">@L["Grid_ColumnFilters"]</span>
    <span class="rg-gridfilter-count" hidden></span>
</button>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The <c>Id</c> of the grid whose filter drawer this button opens — the same string the grid was
    /// given, which the region publishes as <c>data-grid-id</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The grid must also declare <c>FilterEntry="RaptorGridFilterEntry.PageChrome"</c>. The two halves
    /// are checked at runtime, not at compile time: if this button is missing the grid keeps its floating
    /// action button, and if this button names a grid that is not on the page it simply does nothing.
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public string For { get; set; } = default!;
}
